  "abstract": "The KT3b environmental test of Energy-Flow Cosmology returned a null result after four iterations of increasing methodological rigour. We show that the observed monotonic signal collapse across these iterations is consistent with a cross-regime measurement inconsistency, and cannot be uniquely explained by statistical limitations alone. The theoretical prediction (mode activation D_eff) lives in the non-linear galactic regime L2, the environmental driver (rho_env) lives in the linear cosmological regime L1, the observable (R at g ~ a_0) sits on the L1/L2 boundary, and the coupling between regimes (alpha) is not defined as an operator mapping L1 density fields to L2 dynamical response. This constitutes a violation of the Regime-Consistent Measurement Principle (RCMP). We identify the structural failure, classify three valid test architectures (pure L2 RAR shape, pure L1 fsigma8 growth, derived L1->L2 mapping), and argue that the diagnosis is a stronger contribution than the null result itself."
}
